WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.400
Hello.

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:10.050
I'm a professor of psychiatry at Seoul
National University Bundang Hospital.

3
00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:15.430
In this seventh session, we will look at the
rules you need to follow when taking medicine,

4
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.100
common questions, and some myths about medication.

5
00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:25.370
The symptoms of the illness go up and
down, but your treatment must not.

6
00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:30.250
Even when treatment is going well,
symptoms can fluctuate early on.

7
00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:35.690
Recovery happens little by little,
getting worse and better again and again.

8
00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:36.450
Also,

9
00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:42.510
do not stop treatment just because your symptoms
have improved and you think you are cured.

10
00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.580
If you put up with symptoms and
cut down your medicine by force,

11
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.070
you will end up taking more medicine for longer.

12
00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:57.490
To finish treatment, you must reach
remission, a symptom-free state,

13
00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.960
and keep that state steadily.

14
00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.200
If you take the set dose steadily
and your symptoms improve,

15
00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:07.330
the medicine can then be adjusted again.

16
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:12.940
Symptoms of the illness and side
effects of medicine can look alike.

17
00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.980
For example, in depression with excessive sleep,

18
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.720
it is hard to tell whether not being able to get up in

19
00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.820
the morning is due to the medicine or the depression.

20
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.820
It is likely a symptom of the illness
if it is already a known symptom,

21
00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:33.400
gets worse when you feel low and
sluggish, or comes and goes in waves.

22
00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:39.520
It is likely a side effect if it first
appeared after you started the medicine,

23
00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.460
shows up at about the same time
every day after you take it,

24
00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:46.390
or goes away when the dose is reduced.

25
00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:51.610
Rather than judging alone, write
these points down, bring them in,

26
00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:55.100
and sort them out with your doctor.

27
00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:00.370
Stress can make symptoms worse
and can trigger the illness,

28
00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:04.430
but we cannot say that stress
is the cause of the illness.

29
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:10.580
Enough medication makes the mood regulation
circuit stronger and prevents relapse.

30
00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:15.780
Neither medication nor your own
effort alone can beat the illness.

31
00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:20.610
Most medicines are fine to take on an empty stomach.

32
00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:25.590
Usually, take drowsy medicines in the
evening and alerting ones in the morning.

33
00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:29.990
If your doctor gave you a specific
time or method, please follow it.

34
00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.730
The most important thing is to take
it at the same time every day,

35
00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.450
so the level of medicine in your body stays steady.

36
00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:42.050
If you take a bedtime medicine
but tend to fall asleep very late,

37
00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:47.770
take it at a set time between nine and ten
at night rather than right before sleep,

38
00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.590
and go to bed and get up early.

39
00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:56.010
On night shifts, take your bedtime medicine
before your longest sleep after work.

40
00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:00.470
When travelling abroad, take it
at the same hour in local time.

41
00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:05.260
If your work alternates between day
and night, talk with your doctor.

42
00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.080
If you miss a dose, take it as soon as possible.

43
00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.820
But a drowsy medicine can cause
trouble if taken in the morning,

44
00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.000
so it helps to know the features
of your own medicine in advance.

45
00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:23.930
Cold medicine, painkillers and supplements
taken for a short time are mostly fine.

46
00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:30.730
But be sure to tell your doctor about any other
medicines you take and any herbal medicine.

47
00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:34.790
Even if you drank alcohol, you
should still take your medicine.

48
00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:40.450
Heavy drinking can make drowsiness worse, but if
you start skipping medicine because of alcohol,

49
00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.110
treatment cannot succeed.

50
00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:46.610
You need to try to quit or cut down
drinking for the sake of your medicine.

51
00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:50.630
If you run out of medicine, get a prescription quickly,

52
00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:55.730
even from another doctor's clinic
or a nearby psychiatry clinic.

53
00:03:55.750 --> 00:04:02.220
Stopping suddenly can cause side effects, and
it helps to keep a photo of your prescription.

54
00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:07.440
If you are planning a pregnancy, please talk
with your doctor from the planning stage.

55
00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:12.790
It is very important to try to
conceive while your mood is stable.

56
00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:20.290
Depending on the situation, the medicine may be
reduced, switched to a safer one, or, if needed,

57
00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.650
kept after thorough discussion.

58
00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:26.650
It also helps to take folic acid in advance.

59
00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.900
Can medicine really fix the mind?

60
00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:34.960
The body and mind are closely connected,
so when the mind is struggling,

61
00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:38.040
changes in the brain always come with it.

62
00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.990
Medicine can help these changes recover.

63
00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:44.410
Does taking many medicines mean the illness is severe?

64
00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:45.830
Not necessarily.

65
00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:49.070
The number and dose of medicines are mostly decided by

66
00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:52.230
individual differences in how you metabolise drugs,

67
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.760
and by the features of the illness.

68
00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.761
Will I become dependent on medicine?

69
00:04:57.781 --> 00:04:58.289
No.

70
00:04:58.309 --> 00:05:03.567
You use it because you need it until you
have fully recovered, and once you recover,

71
00:05:03.587 --> 00:05:05.918
a time comes when you can manage without it.

72
00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:10.508
How long to continue depends on
things like the number of relapses,

73
00:05:10.528 --> 00:05:13.690
and you decide it together with your doctor.

74
00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.660
Will long-term use lead to addiction?

75
00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.960
Medicines for mood regulation are not addictive.

76
00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:27.400
Some tranquillisers can cause dependence,
but if you use them carefully as prescribed,

77
00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:30.040
you can avoid dependence.

78
00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:35.000
Will long-term use cause dementia
or make me less intelligent?

79
00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:35.500
No.

80
00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:40.300
What raises the risk of dementia is
not the medicine but the mood disorder,

81
00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.350
and the risk actually rises when it is left untreated.

82
00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:48.190
Are there any benefits to taking it for a long time?

83
00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:49.010
Yes.

84
00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:54.230
The medicine not only clears symptoms
but also acts as a protective shield,

85
00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:58.850
so symptoms do not appear even
under fairly ordinary stress.

86
00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:06.720
Take it steadily, as prescribed, and talk with
your doctor about anything you wonder about.

87
00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:09.870
This is the best way to take your medicine.

88
00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:15.730
Next time, we will practise psychotherapy,
a treatment other than medicine,

89
00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.450
and mindfulness together.

90
00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:18.610
Thank you.
